Org-cite is reportedly not very suited for handling large files[1] (at least it wasn't 4 years ago). Suggestions for other packages
- Org-cite per se is not slow, but the =oc-basic= insert processor you're using is on the first load, after which the data is cached.
- citar uses =parsebib=, which is very fast.

You can also limit which parts of the org-cite libraries will load.
- this is actually adjusted in the Lambda Emacs distribution (to deal with any kind of speed issue)
  - Lambda Emacs uses =oc= and =oc-csl= along with =citar=
  - it doesn't make use of =org-ref=
  - the lambda emacs config has changed since 4 years ago and not uses a custom package called =bibtex-capf= (which works with both Markdown and org files)

